<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" dir="ltr" class="h-full bg-gray-100">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex">
    <title>Authorize an application — tectonic plates</title>
    <%= assets(:css) %>
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4">
        <%# This page is reached from claude.ai or ChatGPT and from nowhere on this site, and
            one tap on it hands an API client the account, so the mark at the top is the whole
            of the answer to "am I really on Tectonic". A line of grey 14px text was the
            weakest answer available. The alt is the name rather than "logo" because when the
            image does not draw, that is all that is left to say whose consent screen this is.
            It is deliberately not a link: the only ways out of this flow should be the two
            buttons at the bottom of the form. 224px wide on a phone and 256px from 640px up,
            which reads as a brand mark rather than a favicon without becoming the page. %>
        <img src="/icons/logo.svg" alt="tectonic plates" class="mx-auto mt-6 w-56 sm:w-64">
        <%= yield %>
      </div>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
